From c9a4e3485708b400b7684b7a8763ee7c25dc23f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:08:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(worker): every model_config writer key is a worker
 sidecar key; class failover survives a failed row mirror [daveey]

A managed worker's class failover (402/429 on a class route) mirrored model_routing onto
the session row via session.sidecars; the owner refused the key (invalid_params), the refusal
latched in the receipt journal and close() re-raised it, so the worker exited 1 instead of
answering on the fallback route (run 10210).

- hermes_state_sidecar_keys: one registry for owner validation and the worker pre-check; adds
  model_routing, prompt_refresh_epoch, _fallback_probe_at, reasoning_rejected_carriers,
  onboarding_run, codex_thread_id. Lineage keys stay owner-reserved.
- RuntimeSessionStore.patch_session_model_config refuses an unregistered key before journaling,
  so it fails one call instead of poisoning every later write and the close-time flush.
- try_class_fallback: the row mirror is best-effort; a failure logs and the turn continues.
- tests: AST drift guard over every patch_session_model_config writer; managed-store failover
  wire test (mirror ok / mirror refused); unregistered key does not latch.
---
